# Controls what `gcloud builds submit` UPLOADS to Cloud Build (a different layer
# than .dockerignore, which trims the build CONTEXT once the tarball is on the
# builder). IMPORTANT: when this file exists, gcloud STOPS consulting .gitignore —
# so every sensitive/heavy path that .gitignore covered is re-listed here.
#
# ⚠ This file is the ONLY thing standing between the two deploy paths behaving differently.
# A push-triggered build gets a full repo CHECKOUT and never reads this, so a path missing here
# breaks ONLY `gcloud builds submit` — the documented manual fallback — and only when someone
# reaches for it, which is exactly when something is already wrong. Keep it in lockstep with the
# Dockerfile's COPY list: anything that file needs and this one excludes fails the build at that
# COPY with "file not found in build context" (how `packages/engine` was caught, 2026-07-29).
#
# The apps/api/Dockerfile COPYs the api closure: root package.json, apps/api, .env.production,
# and packages/{db,shared,storage,engine,routing}. Everything else is safe to leave out.

# Dependencies + VCS
**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# SECRETS — never upload. .env.keys holds the dotenvx PRIVATE keys; only the
# encrypted .env.production is needed (and the Dockerfile COPYs it).
.env.keys
.env
.env.development
.env.*.local

# Service-account JSON etc.
keys/
key/
*-sa-key.json

# Not part of the api image closure (the heavy RN tree + unrelated packages).
# `packages/engine` was listed here and is NOT unrelated — the API imports it (roam's
# trigger radii + haversine), so the Dockerfile COPYs it and every `builds submit` died.
apps/mobile
packages/sim
packages/studio

# Build / dev / scratch cruft
dist/
build/
out/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.scratch/
.scratch-audio/
.design-review/
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
